# Frontend Rules — Next.js 14

## Design Tokens — CSS Variables (single source of truth)
All colors and fonts must be defined as CSS variables in `globals.css`. Never hardcode hex values in components.
```css
/* ✅ globals.css */
:root {
  --color-primary: #00B5B8;      /* turquoise blue */
  --color-primary-dark: #008F92;
  --color-secondary: #22C55E;    /* green */
  --color-secondary-dark: #16A34A;

  --font-heading: 'Inter', sans-serif;
  --font-body: 'Inter', sans-serif;
}
```

## UI Components — Single Design System
All base components (Button, Card, Input, Textarea, Toggle, Dropdown, Badge) live in `components/ui/`.
Never create one-off styled versions inline. Extend the `ui/` component instead.
```tsx
// ✅
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/Button';

// ❌ — inline ad-hoc button
<button className="bg-teal-500 px-4 py-2 rounded">...</button>
```

## Icons — Lucide Only
Use `lucide-react` exclusively. No raw SVGs, no other icon libraries.
```tsx
// ✅
import { ShoppingCart, Heart } from 'lucide-react';

// ❌
<svg>...</svg>
```

## Animations — Framer Motion
All transitions and animations use `framer-motion`. No CSS `transition`/`animation` for interactive motion.
```tsx
// ✅
import { motion } from 'framer-motion';
<motion.div initial={{ opacity: 0 }} animate={{ opacity: 1 }} />

// ❌
<div className="transition-opacity duration-300" />
```

## State Management
- Cart, wishlist, UI state → Zustand stores in `lib/store/`
- Never use React `useState` for cart or wishlist — always go through the store
- Server state (products, orders) → fetch via `lib/api/` typed endpoints, not raw `fetch`

## API Calls
All backend calls go through `lib/api/apiFetch`. Never call `fetch()` directly in components.
```tsx
// ✅
import { getProducts } from '@/lib/api/products';

// ❌
const res = await fetch('/api/products');
```

## Auth — JWT in httpOnly Cookie
JWT lives in `httpOnly` cookie only. Never access from `localStorage` or `document.cookie`.
`middleware.ts` reads cookie server-side for route protection.

## Feature Flags
`useFeature` hook fetches flags from backend `/api/features`. Backend is source of truth.
Never hardcode feature states. Never set flags independently from backend response.
```tsx
// ✅
const taxEnabled = useFeature('tax');

// ❌
const TAX_ENABLED = true;
```

## Email — Nodemailer
Transactional emails from Next.js (if any) use Nodemailer. Config via env vars only.

## TypeScript
- Strict mode on. No `any`. Use shared types from `types/`.
- Zod schema per form in `validators/`. Infer TypeScript types from Zod schemas.
```tsx
// ✅
const schema = z.object({ email: z.string().email() });
type FormData = z.infer<typeof schema>;
```

## File Conventions
- Page components: `page.tsx` (App Router)
- Client components: explicit `'use client'` at top
- Default to Server Components — only add `'use client'` when needed (interactivity, hooks, stores)
